package makers:plugin@1.0.0;

/// Reporting that is not output.
///
/// Separate from `artifacts` because these two are the answers to different
/// questions — "what did you produce" and "what should the user know" — and
/// separate from a hook's `error` return because a plugin very often needs
/// to report *many* problems and still finish. A lint plugin that could only
/// signal failure by returning would report its first finding and stop,
/// which is precisely the compiler behaviour everyone turned off with
/// `-fmax-errors`.
interface diagnostics {
    use types.{diagnostic};

    /// Report. The host prefixes the instance name so that several plugins
    /// in one run stay distinguishable, and counts the diagnostic. An
    /// `error` from an instance whose manifest declares
    /// `failure-policy.fatal` sets make's exit status once the analysis pass
    /// completes — deferred rather than immediate, so that all findings are
    /// reported in one run rather than only the first.
    ///
    /// `note` is suppressed unless the run asked for it
    /// (`MAKERS_PLUGIN_VERBOSE`), so a plugin can narrate freely without
    /// making every build noisy.
    ///
    /// Diagnostics currently go straight to stderr. Routing them through
    /// make's own output machinery — so they interleave correctly under `-j`
    /// and honour `--output-sync` — is worth doing and is not done yet; the
    /// analysis pass runs after the update walk, where nothing else is
    /// competing for stderr.
    emit: func(d: diagnostic);
}
